<title>BELGIUM: EU changes intervention wheat quality rules.</title>
<headline>EU changes intervention wheat quality rules.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>An amendment introducing germination tests for intervention wheat was adopted by the European Union's cereals management committee on Thursday, an EU official said.</p>
<p>&quot;The amendment to the regulation (EC 689/92) means that if the germination capacity of wheat going into intervention is less than 85 percent it will be rejected,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>All wheat in EU intervention stores is available for bread making and not for feed and the tests will establish whether wheat is of bread making quality.</p>
<p>The committee did not discuss amendments to legislation on proof of arrival at the market for grain sold out of intervention.</p>
<p>&quot;The item was postponed,&quot; the official said. --Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 6830</p>
</text>
